    "type": "question",
    "label": "27",
    "prompt": "Solve $\\log_2(x)+\\log_2(x^3)=8$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=4$.",
      "worked": "Both logarithms require $x>0$, so the power law applies.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_2(x)+3\\log_2(x)&=8\\\\4\\log_2(x)&=8\\\\\\log_2(x)&=2\\\\x&=2^2=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe value $x=4$ is in the domain and gives $\\log_2(4)+\\log_2(64)=2+6=8$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
